      "label": "Belfast Gazette issue 2382 (Alteration of boundary of Urban County District of Downpatrick (confirmation))",
      "url": "https://www.thegazette.co.uk/Belfast/issue/2382/page/330",
      "note": "16 Sep 1966, page 330. Made 6 Sep 1966. In force: 1 Apr 1967. Confirms Down County Council's order of 16 Jun 1966 extending Downpatrick UD."
    },
    {
      "label": "Ministry of Development Provisional Order Confirmation (Bangor Borough Extension) Act (Northern Ireland) 1966 (1966 c. ii)",
      "url": "https://www.thegazette.co.uk/Belfast/issue/2394/page/465",
      "note": "Local Act confirming the Bangor Borough (Extension) Order (Northern Ireland) 1966. Royal Assent 6 Dec 1966 (Belfast Gazette issue 2394, 9 Dec 1966, page 465). Appointed day 1 Apr 1967, as printed in the confirmed Order. Bangor borough extended; its Princetown, Dufferin, Castle, Clifton and Ballyholme wards were extended."
    },
    {
      "label": "New Towns (Municipal Functions - Craigavon) Order (Northern Ireland) 1967 (S.R. & O. 1967 No. 57)",
      "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisro/1967/57/made",
      "note": "Made under section 28 of the New Towns Act (Northern Ireland) 1965; notice in Belfast Gazette issue 2411, 31 Mar 1967, page 111. From 1 Apr 1967 the Craigavon Development Commission acts as an urban district council for the whole of Lurgan Rural District except Ballyblagh, Knocknashane, Tirsogue and part of Toberhewny, which are added to the Borough of Lurgan; that area is known as the Urban District of Craigavon. The new town was designated by the New Town Designation Order (Northern Ireland) 1965 (Belfast Gazette issue 2317, 6 Aug 1965, page 274), which did not itself alter district boundaries."
    }
